<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Watampone</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Watampone is a town in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulawesi">Sulawesi</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bone-regency">Bone Regency</a> near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-bone">Gulf of Bone</a>. It was the royal seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bugis">Bugis</a> kingdom and later sultanate of Bone, which grew from the 14th century and became a leading power of Sulawesi under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arung-palakka">Arung Palakka</a> in the 17th century.</p></div>
